cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Indy 500 Point-in-Time Probabilistic Decision Support System"
message: "Please cite this repository and the frozen model version used."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Li
    given-names: Fengzhe
repository-code: "https://github.com/fengzhe-li/indy500-point-in-time-decision-support"
version: "FINAL_V3_FROZEN"
date-released: 2026-09-15
abstract: >-
  Physics-conditioned probabilistic performance inference for Indianapolis 500
  qualifying, with explicit historical identifiability, uncertainty
  propagation, and human-in-the-loop scope boundaries (FINAL_V2, the frozen
  scientific core). FINAL_V3 adds a point-in-time application layer on top:
  forecast-vintage provenance, a leakage guard, historical shadow replay,
  evidence-aware abstention, and an isolated hypothetical scenario interface,
  exposed through a FastAPI + React/TypeScript application.

